###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table 5 is captioned 'Testing RMSE error' while its columns say MAE; the column headers are followed (MAE), which is worth a check.
# - The MACE-MP-0 medium and MACE-MP-0b medium checkpoints are not identified by release date, so they are not linked to registry models; they are paper-local runs without training data, as distributed.
# - The silicon errors are stated as 'final RMSE values' after fine-tuning (Fig. 1 shows MAE learning curves). The DFT levels of the HEA and silicon data are not described in the version read.
# - Settings other than the learning rate and epochs (cutoff, correlation order) are MACE defaults and are not stated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

